3]Explain indetail about typecasting ?

	1]Typecasting is the process of converting one datatype into another datatype is called as typecasting
	2]In java thier are 2 types of typecasting:-
		i)implicit typecasting
		ii]explicit typecasting
		
Implicit typecasting:-
======================
->Implicit typecasting is the process of converting the smaller datatypes into larger datatypes is called
as implicit type casting


Explicit typecasting:-
======================
->Explicit typecasting is the process of converting the larger datatypes into smaller datatypes is called as
explicit typecasting, and this has to be done forecefully by the programmer
->During explicit type casting thier is a chance of dataloss


->Among all the 8 primitive datatypes boolean datatype is a datatype which does not participate in
typecasting let it be implicit typecasting or explicit typecasting

->Whenever a char datatype is tried to be converted to other datatype,then that particular character
unicode value will be stored.




4]Is java 100% pure object oriented programming language ?
	->No,java is not 100% pure object oriented programming language because java supports primitive data
	types,although java is not 100% pure object oriented then also we can make java project as 100%
	pure object oriented by making use of a concept called as wrapper classes.
	
->Explain indetail about Wrapper classes ?
	1]In java wrapper class is a class that provides object representation for primitive datatypes
	java includes a set of 8 built in primitive datatypes like boolean,char,byte,short,int,long,float
	and double which represents single value,but this wrapper classes allows this primitive datatypes
	to be treated as objects
	
	2]It supports autoboxing and unboxing
	

AutoBoxing:-
============
	->Autoboxing is the process of automatically converting the primitive datatype into its corresponding
	wrapper class object 
	

UnBoxing:-
==========
	->Unboxing is the process of automatically converting back the object of wrapper class into its
	corresponding primitive datatype.


5]Explain indetail about Strings in java ?

	->A series of characters enclosed in double quotes is called as a String
	->Strings are treated as objects in java,Strings are also known as array of characters
	->In "c" programming language Strings are ended with null character,where as in java programming 
	language Strings are not ended with null character
	->In java thier are 2 types of Strings:-
		i)Immutable Strings
		ii)Mutable Strings
		
		
Immutable Strings:-
===================
	->Immutable Strings are such Strings which cannot be modified after intialization,we can create
	immutable Strings by making use of String class
	->We can create the Strings in 2 ways
		i) by using String literals
		ii) by creating the object for the String class
		
	->The memory allocation for immutable Strings will take place inside the String constant pool of heap
	area
	->Whenever we create the String by making use of String literals then the String will be created in
	String constant pool
	->Duplicates are not allowed inside the String constant pool
	->Whenever we create the String by creating the object for the String class,then the String will be
	created in heap area
	->Duplicates are allowed inside the heap area
	
->In java thier are 4 different ways of comparing the Strings:-
	1]== will always check for the references of the String
	2]equals() will always check for the String values
	3]equalsIgnoreCase() method will ignore the case and then check for the String values
	4]compareTo() is used to compare the Strings character by character and then decide that which
	String is greater,here the comparision will happens based on the unicode value of the character
	
	
->If String values are concatinated then the String will be created in String constant pool
->while performing concatination if String references are used then always the String will be created in
heap area

->intern() is used to copy the String from heap area to String constant pool


->If we try to modify the immutable String then the new String object will be created and previous String
object will remains same as it is.

->Stringtokenizer is an inbuilt class which is coming from java.util package
->Stringtokenizer is used to chop the Strings at the specified character in the token.


Mutable Strings:-
=================

	->Mutable Strings are such Strings which can be modified after intialization
	->To create Mutable Strings thier are 2 classes in java:-
		i)StringBuffer
		ii)StringBuilder
	->StringBuffer class and StringBuilder class in java is used to create the mutable sequence of
	characters but their are few key difference between StringBuffer class and StringBuilder class
	

1]Synchronization
	->StringBuffer is synchronized meaning it is thread safe,mutliple threads can access the method of
	StringBuffer without causing the concurrence issue
	->This comes up with performance overhead due to synchronization
	
	->StringBuilder is not synchronized meaning it is not thread safe,it is used when thread safety is
	not a concern,as this performs faster than StringBuffer due to lack of synchronization overhead
	
	
2]Performance
	->StringBuffer is slower than StringBuilder because of synchronization
	->StringBuilder is faster than StringBuffer because it does not have synchronization
	

3]Usage
	->We use StringBuffer to modify the Strings in multithreaded enviornment where thread safety is a 
	concern
	->We use StringBuilder to modify the Strings in single threaded environment where thread safety is 
	 not a concern
	 
	 
StringBuffer and StringBuilder are inbuilt classes ,so they has inbuilt methods like:-
	1]append()
	2]insert()
	3]reverse()
	4]replace()
	5]delete()
	6]toString()
	7]capacity()
	
	
StringBuffer and StringBuilder has default capacity of 16



**** Why Strings are immutable ? ****
	->String class is immutable in java because it improves the performance and speed up the String
	operations,it enables string pooling,optimize memory usage and prevents security vulnerabilties and
	ensure thread safety.
	
	

